1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elisabet Håkansdotter Hand, (Nr.59)=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabet Hand, (född 1598, död 10 april 1651) var först frilla åt hertig Johan av Östergötland och gifte sig senare med överstelöjtnanten Per Joensson (död 19 mars 1664) som 1632 adlades med namnet Gyllensvärd och blev stamfar för
2 CONC  släkten med detta namn. Deras dotter, Virginia Gyllensvärd, var gift med Johan Gustafsson Örnevinge.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006257517150&photo_id=6000000168182462079&position=0 '''Daughter of Håkan Hand (Knutsson) (- 1633) &  Virginia Vasa (Eriksdotter) (1559 - 1633)''']
2 CONT * Håkan Knutsson's and Virginia Eriksdotter's daughter Elisabeth Hand (born 1588, died April 10, 1651) was first in relationship with Duke Johan of Östergötland and later married the Lieutenant Colonel Per Jönsson (died March 19, 
2 CONC 1664), who in 1632 was named Gyllenswaard and became the ancestor of the family. with that name. Their daughter, Virginia Gyllenswaard, was married to Johan Gustafsson Örnevinge. 
2 CONT * Born: 1598 in Odensjö, Småland, Kronoberg county, Sweden
2 CONT * Elizabeth Hand, (born 1598, died 10 April 1651) 
2 CONT * In letters to Axel Oxelstierna April 24, 1618 and May 10, 1618 from then Bishop Johan Rotovius in Angelstad, Elisabet has been deceived and has been humiliated by Duke Johan of Östergötland, who was Johan III's son and married t
2 CONC o his cousin Karl IX's daughter.   Elisabet and Per received 5 children: Beata, Knut, Virginia, Johan and Märta.
2 CONT * Johan would have stayed in Björkenäs at the New Year 1612 where county accommodation could be offered during the fighting against the Danes in western Sweden.
2 CONT * Mourning in the house, wife Elisabeth Hand "passes away" - On April 10, 1651, there is mourning in the house, because then Per Gyllensvärd's wife Elisabeth dies. According to unconfirmed sources, Elisabeth Hand was buried in the
2 CONC  old Hössna church and laid in the choir.
2 CONT * Death:	April 10, 1651 (53) in Önnarp, Hössna, Västergötland, Älvsborgs county, Sweden  
2 CONT * Buried:	1651-11-30 Hössna, Hössna church
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Hand_nr_59 '''Per Joensson Gyllensvärd,'''] son of Joen Pehrsson.  Elisabet was first mistress To Duke John of Östergötland and Later Married Lieutenant Colonel Per Joensson (d. 19 
2 CONC march 1664) as 1632 Knighted with the name Gyllensvärd and Was stamfar for the family with this name. Their daughter, Virginia Gyllensvärd, was married to Johan Gustafsson Örnevinge. Per Joenson is buried in Hössna Church, so also
2 CONC  his wife, who died already on 10 April 1651.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Johan Persson''' born 1617. Rider. Death 1688. Johan , (son of Per Joensson, adlad Gyllenswaard), to Sunnaryd and Bolstad (Bolmstad) in Bolmsö parish, Gavlö in Dannäs parish (all in Jönköping County) and Priesttorp in Berga p
2 CONC arish, Kronoberg county. Born 1617-05-13. Be a fan of Småland's riders 1635 2 . Lieutenant there. 1636 2 . Rider champion 1644 2 –1655, from 1646 as reformed. Died 1688-02-02. His coat of arms was erected in Bolmsö old church in S
2 CONC måland and, at the expense of members of the family in 1926, was restored in the restored 1839 church. Married to Märta Stierna , daughter of rider champion Måns Stierna and Anna Siöblad .
2 CONT *''' Knut Persson''' Regimental Quartermaster. Knut , (son of Per Joensson, adlad Gyllenswaard). Was a member of the Jönköping Regiment in 1644. Transp. to Colonel Silfverhielm's regiment 1645. Regiment Quartermaster at the Dutch 
2 CONC Regiment. Died in 1664 (shortly before 12/4) and buried In Hössna church Älvsborg county. Married to Eufrosyne Lillie af Aspenäs in her 1st marriage (married 2nd before 1674 to Captain Gustaf Silfverlåås ), daughter of the Lieuten
2 CONC ant Colonel Peder Lillie af Aspenäs , and Maria Amalia von Lepel.
2 CONT *''' Virginia Persdotter,''' lived as a widow in 1685.  Married in 1641 with substitute Johan Gustafsson , left Örnevinge in his 1st wedding, died in 1685.
2 CONT * '''Märta Persdotter,''' to Önnarp, which was reduced to 1689 from her, born 1620, died 1694-11-11 Önnarp Married to Captain Jonas Larsson Silfverswärd , died in 1656.
2 CONT *''' Beata Persdotter''' Lived widow in 1698. Married to the major Jöns Svinhufvud in Västergötland, (no.199), born circa 1621 in Önnarp.Hossna, Åsundenleden, Sweden & died on November 11, 1698 in Laxarby, i Steneby (P), Sweden.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Hand_nr_59 Håkan Knutsson Hand, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Knutsson Hand (son of Knut Håkansson. Died 1633 at Vret. Married around 1586 to Virginia Eriksdotter , natural daughter of King Erik XIV and Agda Persdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Catharina Hand.''' Married 1615 to the governor Johan Henriksson Rytter .
2 CONT * '''Knut Hand.''' Unmarried murdered in the beginning of is 1614 at Rugils in Russia.
2 CONT * '''Sofia Hand,''' lived 1634. Married to Lieutenant Colonel Baltsar von Neüman .
2 CONT * '''Arvid Hand.''' Died unmarried 1621.
2 CONT * '''Erik Hand.''' Died unmarried 1632-08-30 in Ingolstadt. Colonel.
2 CONT * '''Johan Hand.''' District Chief. died before 1656. District chief, captain. Married to Agneta Gyllenmärs , daughter of Admiral Olof Andersson ( Gyllenmärs ) and Kerstin Bröms .Children :Virginia Hand, died 1681. Married to Colo
2 CONC nel Nils Lilliehöök af Fårdala.
2 CONT * '''Elisabet Hand,''' born 1598, died 1651-04-10. Married to Lieutenant Colonel Per Joensson Gyllensvärd .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hand_(sl%C3%A4kt) Hand (Relative) Swedish Noble Family, no.59, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hand was a Swedish noble family descended from the savior Håkan Persson in Västergötland , died around 1530.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son was the lieutenant Knut Håkansson , who distinguished himself in the Russian war in the 1550s and during the Nordic Seven Years' War and fell in the Battle of Axtorna on October 20, 1565.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, the bailiff and district chief Håkan Knutsson (died 1595 or 1596), was married to Erik XIV 's illegitimate daughter Virginia Eriksdotter .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.hembygd.se/h-ssna-hembygdsf-rening/plats/316540/text/59389 Önnarp Area]
2 CONT
2 CONT In the land register of 1542, Önnarp is recorded as two farms, which in everyday speech had no special names. At the beginning of the 17th century, the names Stora and Lilla Önnarp were used. The first known owner of the farm, whi
2 CONC ch was then called Öndarp, was Håkan Larsson. He was "kiyrkiowärjande" (churchwarden) in Hössna church during a bishop's visitation in 1554. At the end of the 16th century and the beginning of the 17th century, the bailiff Lars Hå
2 CONC kansson and his wife Kirstin Mårtensdotter owned the farm. Lars probably died in 1614 and was buried in it grave, which the couple prepared for themselves in Hössna's old church. It is their tombstone, which stands to the right of
2 CONC  the old sacristy door. The widow Kirstin Månsdotter sold Önnarp Skattegård in 1626 to her neighbor, manly captain Peder Joensson. This Peder Joensson was later ennobled and became lieutenant colonel Peder (Per) Joensson Gyllensvä
2 CONC rd. In 1629, he received salvation on the farm Önnarp and other farms in Hössna parish and formed the manors of Önnarp and Hössna Åkerby today. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Önnarp's manor was then inherited by his daughter Märta, who was married to Silversvärd. She owned and farmed the farm until the reduction in 1689, when the manor was transferred to the crown.
2 CONT In the 18th century, Önnarp had several farmers, as well as the Flack and Posse families as owners, before Lieutenant Wästfält bought it around 1775. He sold the farm in 1788 for 3,122 Riksdaler to the German-born Major Ludvig von
2 CONC  Braun, married to Hedvig von Staffeldt. Major von Braun died on 12 Nov. 1805 and his wife much later. They are both buried in the old cemetery. A nephew of Ludwig von Braun was the well-known poet Wilhelm von Braun, who in his yo
2 CONC unger days stayed at Önnarp. Among other things, he has written the poem I låga ryttartorpet 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the first half of the 19th century, the farm was owned by, among others, the Schotte family. One of the sons in the family drowned one summer day in the North Sea. As late as the 1920s, a memorial to the Schotte family hung
2 CONC  in Hössna church. There were two crossed swords with royal name slate.
2 CONT CF Colliander then bought Önnarp for a barrel of gold, whose value at the time was 100,000 dalers silver coins or 16,666 rdr 32 shillings national debt. Colliander in turn sold the farm to the mayor of Ulricehamn J. Bäckström for 
2 CONC the same amount. After his death, the farm was bought in 1856 by OP Rylander from Brostorp. Later, the son Johan Olof Rylander became the owner of the farm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During JO Rylander's time, Önnarp once again experienced a period of glory. At that time, a dairy, mill, distillery, bone mill for the production of bone meal and a sawmill were built. The latter consisted of a frame saw with a si
2 CONC ngle blade, a so-called one-burner. In addition, the Älvsborg county agricultural school was run under the auspices of the Husthalningssällskapet, whose director was the owner of the farm, JO Rylander.
2 CONT He was a very prominent man and was elected to the first chamber of the Riksdag, where he remained until his death in 1907. He was buried at Timmele cemetery. continued see Önnarp Herrgård
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =History 1=
2 CONT
2 CONT Hand was a Swedish nobility derived from the savior Håkan Persson in Västergötland , died around 1530. His son was the chiefsman Knut Håkansson , who featured in the Russian war in the 1550s and during the Nordic Seven-Year War an
2 CONC d plunged into the Battle of Axtorna on October 20, 1565. The son of Da Håkan Knutsson, the fiancé and chieftain, died in 1595 or 1596, married to Erik XIV 's extramarital daughter, Virginia Eriksdotter, and was the father of Colo
2 CONC nel Erik Hand (1632) who was wounded and captured during the fighting outside Nuremberg in the summer of 1632 and died in captivity . [ 1 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Knutsson's and Virginia Eriksdotter's daughter Elisabeth Hand (born 1598, died April 10, 1651) was first dear to Duke Johan of Östergötland and later married the Lieutenant Colonel Per Joensson (dead 19 March 1664), who was 
2 CONC named Gyllensvärd in 1632 and became ancestor of the family with this name. Their daughter, Virginia Gyllensvärd, was married to Johan Gustafsson Örnevinge .
2 CONT
2 CONT A son of Knut Håkansson, Arvid Knutsson, called himself Drake, and that family was introduced to the Riddarhuset under the name Drake of Hagelsrum .
2 CONT
2 CONT =History 2=
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Joensson , Gyllensvärd left, to Önnarp, and Hössna, both in Hössna, the county of Älvsborg. From Sunnerbo, in Småland. Adopted war service 1607, was a fighter at Västbo krektar 1618-03-26 and was 1622 at the Riga Lieutenant in
2 CONC  his brother-in-law Baltzar von Neuman's company of Swag Johan Hindersson Routers of Skälboö Regemente Västgöta Knektar (Skaraborg regemente). The captain of Nils Ribbing's West Govtegemente (Älvsborgs) 1624. Transfered to Västgöt
2 CONC a rider 1628. Patterned as a rider at Smålands rider 1630-06-17 in Kalmar. Admitted 1632-08-12 in the field camp at Nuremberg, but the nobility letter first signed 1634-09-10 and confirmed 1647-04-20 (introd. 1638-01-17 under numb
2 CONC er 240). Major 1632, at the end of the year. Lieutenant Colonel 1633 and then brought in nine with top tenants commanded over the regiment during the visit of Lützen, Fredrik Stenbock, at home in the country. Exit from the Registr
2 CONC y in 1641, when he was not appointed to his Colonel. Head of a nobility company at the outbreak of the war with Denmark in 1644, contributing substantially to the successful outcome of the battle at Önsvalla Pass in Halland. Dismi
2 CONC ssed 1656. Death 1664-03-19 and buried in the midsummer's day in Hössna church. He bought 1626 Önnarps tax yard, etc. in Hössna socken, and received 1629-03-03 peace of mind in a pleasant time. During the following three decades h
2 CONC e formed through the purchase of the tax and krono home in Västergötland and Småland the seas Önnarp and Hössna as well as Prästtorp in the Berga parish, Kronoberg County. [ 1 ]. Married to Elisabet Hand , to Hössna and Gavlö, bor
2 CONC n 1598, died 1651-04-10 and buried in Hössna church, daughter of the governor Håkan Hand , and Virginia, King Erik XIV's natural daughter with Agda Persdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT =History 3=
2 CONT
2 CONT Gyllensvärd or Gyllenswärd, is a Swedish surname originating from Captain Per Joensson from Jönköping, married to Erik XIV and Agda Persdotter 's granddaughter Elisabeth Hand to Hössna and Gavlö.
2 CONT
2 CONT As elder felt tribal father was previously reported a time-shoemaker by the name of Joen Persson, but later genealogy has been able to derive the ancestry further back, to an Jon in Gavlö in Dannäs parish in Jönköping County who w
2 CONC as county and mentioned in the sources around 1550. A grandson of him, Per Joensson (d. 19 March 1664), earned himself up to Rittmeister at Smålands Cavalry and later Lieutenant colonel. To wife he should have had Elisabeth Hand o
2 CONC f the family No. 59 whose mother Virginia Eriksdotter according to Anrep was frillodotter to King Erik XIV and Agda persdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Joensson knighted in 1632 during a campaign in Nuremberg (probably the Battle of Alte Veste), but without obtaining a noble name or weapon, then Gustav Adolphus never signed the nobility letter. With Axel Oxenstierna good memo
2 CONC ry, his exaltation in the noble stallion was confirmed and Sköldebrevet signed by the Trustees of the government 1634. The name he took on the introduction in 1638, when the family got the number 240. Finally, his nobility confirm
2 CONC ed was in a letter by Queen Kristina 1647.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through acquisitions formed Gyllensvärd the Manor Önnarp and Hössna, associated Hössna parish in Västergötland in Ulricehamnstrakten and the vicarage in Berga and Gavlö in Dannäs Parish, not far east of Bolmen in Småland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Joenson is buried in Hössna Church, so also his wife, who died already on 10 April 1651.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''John, Rittmeister,'''
2 CONT * '''Knut,''' Regimental District Champion
2 CONT *''' Virginia,''' lived widow. Married 1641 to Mats Johan Gustafsson, ennobled Örnevinge.
