1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingrid Paulina=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Petrus Paulinus (Paulin Hilletan Lilliengrip Lillienstam) and Botilda Jönsdotter Falk 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Lannerstierna_nr_1592?fbclid=IwAR3o99rLc2wiRhV7mcrc7g3jXN9yBRB4sa2fv_uM8fZMYabEG8e6l7qhBb4 Noble family Lannerstierna no. 1592, by Adelsvapen Genealogies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jonas Lannerus,''' Supposed to have been a lecturer (in Växjö?) and married to a daughter of the bishop of Växjö diocese Nils Krokius.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Abrahamus Jonæ Lannerus,''' born 1638-09-21 in Växjö. Student in Turku 1660, in Uppsala 1665-04-11 and in Lund 1669-03-15, where he disp. for the degree and became mag. s. å. Ordained priest in Lund 1671-08-25. War Priest. Pa
2 CONC stor in Skatelöv's pastorate of Växjö diocese in 1678. Died 1697-04-07/4 [Vsn]. Married to Ingrid Paulin , born 1645 1 , died 1721-09-11, probably daughter of the vicar in Hinneryd's pastorate of the said diocese Petrus Paulinus a
2 CONC nd Botilda Jonsdotter Falk. 2
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peter Lannière ,''' ennobled Lannerstierna, born 1680-09-22 in Skatelöv's vicarage, Kronoberg County. Student in Uppsala 3 1695-08-23. Volunteer at the life guard in 1700. Field sergeant at Småland's three-man infantry regime
2 CONC nt, s. å. Adjutant there. 1701. Ensign 1702-05-13. Second lieutenant at Hälsinge regiment 1705-03-04. First lieutenant there. 4 1708-12-05. Captain at Kronoberg's regiment 1709-11-12. Resignation 1710-07-30. Commandant in Hälsingb
2 CONC org 1711-03-01. Major's character 4sd Confirm.completion 1715-05-23. Knighted 1717 1/2 (introd. 1720 under no. 1592). Character of lieutenant colonel 17-12-1717. Colonel and commandant in Landskrona 1742-07-06. Died there 1748-03-
2 CONC 23 ​​and buried on 2/4. 'He made an unexpected incursion of the Russians into the city of Mitau, on the night between July 12 and 13, 1705, with a small assembled party, the enemy made a brave resistance, drove back two troops and
2 CONC  recaptured four Swedish regimental pieces of metal, but in doing so had both the leg pipes on right leg broken off by a poisoned bullet, from which for 1 3/4 years he endured much pain and finally had to have the leg removed and 
2 CONC use wooden legs'. Married 1704-07-01 in Libau in Courland to Catharina de Lyes , born 1683-01-06 in the said town, died 1736-04-26 in Hälsingborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT
