1 OCCU Soldier and Farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rasmus Gotskalksson was born in 1694 in Håland, Etne. He was the owner of the largest farm in Indre Håland after it was split up in 1715. Rasmus was a soldier and first came home from the war in 1720. While he was 
2 CONC gone his mother and brother Elling ran the farm. When his wife Siri died in 1721 he had a wealth of 128 rdlr and a debt of 148 rdlr. In 1725 and 1735 he bought land that his father had passed down to other relatives. But in 1736 t
2 CONC he land was once again split up - something he took hard and resulted with him selling all the land he owned in Håland in 1751 to Kristen/Christen Hansson Frette. In his last years he co-managed his son's (Gotskalk) farm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His first marriage was to Siri Torsdotter b 1684 d 1721 whom had a son outside wedlock from earlier - named Sæbjørn Hallvardsson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Etnesoga II page 383
